    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You have a military rank from your career as a soldier. Soldiers loyal to your former military organization still recognize your authority and influence, and they defer to you if they are of a lower rank. You know your way around military etiquette, and so long that people think you are an active member, you can invoke your rank to exert influence over other soldiers and requisition simple equipment or vehicles for temporary use. You can also usually gain access to friendly military bases where your rank is recognized.</p>",
